---
// The frame shared by the diagrams in the guides: the drawing on the surface color, and a caption that says in words
// what it shows. The drawing is HTML, so its text stays real text; the frame is the size container that decides
// whether a flow stacks or lines up in a row.
---

<figure class="idn-figure not-content">
  <div class="canvas"><slot /></div>
  <figcaption><slot name="caption" /></figcaption>
</figure>
